  "goodToKnow": "Der Säugling is an infant, a baby in its first year, the formal and medical term; everyday German says das Baby. It comes from saugen (to suck, nurse), as does das Säugetier (mammal). Then comes das Kleinkind (toddler). Nouns ending in -ling are masculine: der Liebling, der Flüchtling, der Lehrling. German parents receive Elterngeld for up to 14 months when they care for a Säugling. Plural: die Säuglinge."
